    "Where SteamHead has taught. This file drives the Atlas map's country labels,",
    "region highlights, and city dots. Edit it, then re-run `npm run build`.",
    "",
    "INCOMPLETE — James's list of 2026-09-02 with known gaps, marked TODO below.",
    "",
    "highlight:  'regions' = fill only the listed admin-1 units (big countries)",
    "            'whole'   = fill the whole country (small countries)",
    "            'none'    = no fill; the label and city dots carry it",
    "status:     'taught' = we have run classes here",
    "            'planned' = booked or coming soon (drawn as a hollow outline)",
    "regions:    Natural Earth admin-1 `name` values, exactly as spelled there.",
    "label:      short name for the on-screen label. Keep it SHORT — this is read",
    "            from 30 feet. 'USA' not 'United States of America'.",
    "label_at:   [lng, lat] anchor for the label. Omit to use the country centroid.",
    "leader:     true = draw a short line from the label to the country (used for",
    "            the crowded European cluster, where labels sit out in the water).",
    "",
    "Nothing in this file is private data: cities and countries only, no schools,",
    "no people, no rosters (see docs/decisions.md D6)."
